/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/field-collision.mem:51:''did:webvh built this exact split and shipped it.'' It stands as the one deployed method pairing ledger-free pre-rotation (`nextKeyHashes` — commit the HASH of the next authorized key, so a stolen current key cannot seize succession, the twin of `nextHandleKeyDigest`) WITH an in-protocol witness+watcher layer: witnesses threshold-gate an update (`did-witness.json`), while ''watchers are non-voting monitors that cache the DID Log and detect equivocation'' (identity.foundation/didwebvh/v1.0). Its self-certifying id (SCID) survives a full host move, and `portable:true`+`alsoKnownAs` give credible exit — a near-twin of the handle-KEL + Meshpalace-watcher + severability design, arrived at independently. And its watchers ride ON THE PUBLISHED DOCUMENT (`watchers:[url]`, webhooks in the log): the KEL stays minimal while the ''handle CARD names the watchers that sighted a head'', handing a reader a starting set to compare against — the CONIKS per-reader compare, with a discovery hint.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/field-collision.mem:74:* ''SSB's FROZEN IDENTITY (the builder-risk we already escaped).'' Secure Scuttlebutt bound identity to ONE keypair on an append-only log and shipped NO rotation: a compromised key appends to your log forever; the only cure mints a NEW identity, losing every social tie. ''Here lies the grave of getting succession wrong under carriage.'' We escaped it BY CONSTRUCTION — the name binds a ROLLING QUORUM (the k-of-n HandleGlamour), not a fixed key; the rolling recovery commitment + armed inception supply the KERI-pre-rotation SSB lacked. Note it as the thing our design exists to avoid.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/field-collision.mem:100:* ''KERI VINDICATES the handle-KEL, mechanism-for-mechanism.'' A signed key-event-log with inception / rotation / interaction; acceptance by ''TOAD — Threshold of Accountable Duplicity, N≥2F+1'' — the SAME accept-on-witness-quorum the leased-projection compare-and-swap performs (extend only when the board head still reads as the head last folded). KERI ''pre-rotation'' (commit only the DIGEST of the next key-set; a later rotation reveals the preimage) hardens rotate / burn against a DEAD attacker holding current keys, and belongs in the verb family. ⚠ It defends ONLY the dead attacker: a LIVE capture of current+next keys has NO administrative recovery in KERI (the exposure below). vLEI runs; "in production at scale" stays [verify].
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/live-equivocation.mem:35:* ''The DEAD-key thief'' breaks a drawer and finds a key you STOPPED using. ''KERI pre-rotation already defeats them'' — the key they hold cannot authorize its own succession; you rotated past it. The FACE rung handles this.
