/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/node/herm-carriage.mem:11:role        = "invariant law: WHERE a herm stands its floor gates, HOW they answer, and the GATE-NATIVE carriage pull a vessel hands its carriage. A herm stands a floor gate at the explicit Nexus it was joined to and only there — a Nexus whose carriage board, on its own replica, counts a `carry` for its own vessel key (the shut-routes house ruling, stable-founding-road #/rulings: an explicit Nexus opens the herm relay). There it answers any proven peer that knocked (operator ruling \"A herm answers the knock\"). It signs its floor pin with the carried key and lays the statement on its own replica of the board. A reader presents its counted carry or its worn face with its admit; nothing composed, nothing dialed."
