packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:1:/**
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:2: * place-floor-pin — a PLACE's floor pin, carried where a reader already holds the Nexus that carries the place, and the
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:3: * place's own presentation at that Nexus's floor gates.
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:4: *
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:5: * WHY A PLACE SIGNS ITS OWN PIN. A herm stands a floor gate only at a Nexus whose quorum counted a `carry` act over the
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:6: * herm's own vessel key (`placeCarriedNexuses`). Its floor pin derives from its floor key, which no seat holds, so no seat
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:7: * can mint it; and an announcement never authenticates its own first pin (house ruling "The admit's gate pin"). So the
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:8: * herm signs ONE statement per Nexus with the key the quorum's act names: `{ kind, placeKey, nexus, route, tier, digest }`
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:9: * over the pin it stands there. A reader files that pin only when
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:10: *
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:11: *   1. the statement reads whole, its pin reads whole, at floor tier, at the Nexus the reader asked, on the route asked;
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:12: *   2. the place's signature verifies under `placeKey`, over this exact image (domain-separated from every other seal);
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:13: *   3. the reader's OWN held root of that Nexus counts a `carry` for `placeKey` (the carrier fold over its own replica).
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:14: *
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:15: * The quorum's act authenticates the key; the key authenticates the pin. A statement for an uncarried key, a pin of
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:16: * another Nexus or route, or a torn signature files nothing. The statement rides the Nexus's carriage board beside the acts
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:17: * (a sidecar keyed by the place key, which the act extractor skips), so any replica writer may carry it and none can forge
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:18: * it (lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/place-floor-pin, whose status line names its standing).
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:19: *
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:20: * OWED (the carrier's #/owed): the statement carries no causal position, and the pair index holds no replace, so an older
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:21: * valid statement can stand in for a newer one after a floor-key rotation until the index drops it.
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:22: *
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:23: * THE PLACE ARM. A place presents the quorum's counted `carry` act over its own key at the gate's Nexus, with every
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:24: * counted act of that relation in its causal past as the lineage the gate's reader walks (`verifyPresentedCarry`). The
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:25: * head is the counted `carry` no other counted act of this place descends from; a counted `uncarry` that descends from it
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:26: * leaves the place with no arm to present.
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:27: *
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:28: * Meme: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/place-floor-pin
packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts:29: */
