bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:340:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:341:!! OWED ~ what the code holds, and what stays unproven
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:342:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:343:''What stands in code'': the leaf identity loads the vessel's seed and ContactCard (`packages/lararium-node/src/leaf-identity.ts`); the auth wire binds a presentation to the vessel key (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/auth-wire.ts`); the node gate sends `lar:challenge` before any proof (`packages/lararium-node/src/daemon-auth-gate.ts`); the PersonaGroup ring looks up grants by vessel key, and its own-hand path skips the check (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-group-ring.ts`); the sibling proof sends a device edge inside its sealed box (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/leaf-peer-proof.ts`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:344:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:345:''What stands specified in code.'' Each names a module and its vectors, and no production path calls any of them, so none reads as built (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/working-procedures#/wiring-an-unreached-module">>). Each stays out of its package's barrel until its caller lands.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:346:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:347:* ''The subjects'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-proof-subjects.ts`): the typed keys, the scope, the certificate and its request, the withdrawal event, the frontier, the session certificate, every signed image, and a reader for each. Every key and signature passes the one door (`ed25519-door.ts`); the purposes stand in the domain table (`domains.ts`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:348:* ''Private authority'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-authority.ts`): minting, the request, the certificate, the withdrawal, the fold of a reader's memory, and the chain check with its six verdicts. Its callers: the fleet-join door, the removal door and the gate. It also reads a vessel's OWN chain with no session key in it (`checkVesselChain`), which a session opens on.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:349:* ''The session signer'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-signer.ts`). Its callers: the node's session open on the local socket, and the browser holder. One door opens a session and mints its signer (`openSignedSession`), so no session stands live without one.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:350:* ''The gate bundle'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`): the floor and sovereign tiers with their typed routes and roots (the serving tier stands owed with the ember's train E), the pin, its digest, the knock, the prologue, and the transport and signing keys one gate derives per (tier, Nexus, route). Nothing rests. Its caller: the vessel's gate composer.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:351:* ''The exchange's subjects'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-exchange.ts`): the presentation and the answer with their readers, the image of the finish, the image of the verdict, the browser's first-flight envelope with its reader and its refusals (#/the-browser-envelope), and the house's sealed frame layout.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:352:* ''The gate'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-gate.ts`): the whole exchange against a socket and the collaborators it asks: a deadline source, an admit reader over the one presenter-verifier, the shadow ring, the grant ring, the sorter, a withdrawal memory and a session table. Every silence names ONE reason from the gate's fixed vocabulary on the vessel's own log (`GATE_SILENCE_REASONS`), with at most one detail drawn from a vocabulary the gate already types; no thrown error's text and no string a collaborator spelled reaches that log. A first flight of any length but 96 bytes draws silence before any Noise work. Its caller: the socket cutover.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:353:* ''The dialers'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-dial.ts`): the other half of the exchange, for a face and for a faceless place, one function each for a node and a browser. Their callers: both client transports, at the cutover.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:354:* ''The gate's stored memory'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-withdrawal-store.ts`): one row of signed events per face key, verified again at every load, accreting under one writer. Its caller: the gate composer, over rows the vessel seals.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:355:* ''The session face supplier'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-face.ts`): it joins a verified chain, this vessel's own key for the face, the admit's verdict and the private grant into the face a session wears, and verifies none of the last three itself (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/what-a-session-carries">>). Its callers: the same two.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:356:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:357:''What those modules need that nothing supplies yet'':
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:358:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:359:* ''Two custody rows.'' The face proof key rests cold with the root holder, one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus); a vessel's face-scoped key rests hot on its own vessel, one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus). Each holds 32 secret bytes and reads whole or refuses by name. The modules name the rows and the two signing doors they ask of the custody seat, and write no row.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:360:* ''The admit's own mark.'' The supplier reads the presenter-verifier's verdict over an admit and checks it against the chain. The admit's quorum signs a commitment to what it carries (`carriageCommit`), and the held-root door hands back the head of the admitted nym's key line, which the supplier holds against the chain's face key; the verdict itself still carries no mark a caller cannot spell by hand. A chain another vessel presented verifies as well as this vessel's own, so the session opener also owes the supplier the key its own custody row names.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:361:* ''The private grant's reader.'' The record that binds a face key to its PersonaGroup at one Nexus rests in the group's private causal state, and the ring reads it by vessel key today.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:362:* ''Where a face's own history rests on its vessels'': in the face's private causal state. A gate's own memory rests in its vessel store (#/the-withdrawal-proof).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:363:* ''The floor and sovereign roots' doors'' stand at their seats (the serving key's door stands owed with train E), and no composer calls them until the socket cutover. A floor bundle asks the floor key's derive door (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`), which answers while the vessel rests locked, hands back a fresh child its caller overwrites and never the floor key. A sovereign bundle asks the custody seat's (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`), which answers only while the seat holds its key. The two doors carry two types, so a line that hands one tier's door to the other fails to compile; a root refuses a door of the other tier and a door no mint made by name (`door-other-tier`); and each seat's door refuses the other tier's child by name. A door states only what its minter claimed, so one weld holds the minters to the two seats: a second caller of either mint, anywhere in source, turns it red (`packages/lararium-node/tests/gate-root-door-minters.test.ts`). The composer owes the call.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:364:* ''Sealed rows for the gate's memory'' stand at the custody seat, and no gate calls them until the socket cutover. The store asks a door for one row of bytes by name (`gateMemoryRows`, `packages/lararium-node/src/gate-memory-rows.ts`): one row per face key in the vessel's storage home, named by the proof-subject digest, sealed under the vessel key through the seat's one-holder update door. One holder answers one door, so the gates of one composition share one writer; and a write that lacks an event the row holds refuses while the row keeps its bytes. A locked vessel reads none and refuses by name; a row that stands and does not open, or opens to anything but a list of events, refuses at the read and at the write, its bytes never move, and the gate that asked falls silent. The store drops its view of a row whose write the door refused and verifies that row again. The seat holds no counter a restored disk could not also restore, so the door adds no fence against a rollback (#/the-withdrawal-proof). The row belongs to its vessel, and no face's backup bundle carries it. The composer owes the call.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:365:* ''A held Nexus root per gate'': the roster, the charter lineage, the deny board and the antigen that the admit reader folds, with the causal position it read them at. A gate that holds no root refuses every admit by name.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:366:* ''The rings by face key.'' The shadow ring owes a reading over one presenter (set aside at this gate; set aside from this vessel's own fleet), and the grant ring owes the private record by face key. Both read by vessel key today.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:367:* ''The sorter over proven facts'': a class from a held admit, a private grant, the fleet reading and the arm as presented, over ONE Nexus's posture.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:368:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:369:''Unproven, and each blocks the part that rests on it'':
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:370:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:371:* ''The envelope beyond the measured run'': through TLS, through HTTP/2, on a phone's own engine and behind other proxies (#/the-browser-envelope). The token's syntax, its bound and the terminator's log stand measured and fixed.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:372:* ''The sealed frames' layout'': the frame that carries the gate's handshake reply, and the frames that carry a presentation, a frontier and the events beside it. They ride binary WebSocket messages no proxy reads; the layout in `gate-exchange.ts` stands as the house's own; the cutover has landed, and roadmap row `W28` freezes it before the founding bake.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:373:* ''The withdrawal proof under a live partition.'' The fold and the six verdicts stand proven as pure functions over synthetic histories, and the six answers stand proven at one gate against a dialer in the same process, partitioned by hand. No two gates and no real herm have yet carried one.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:374:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:375:''OWED ~ seven debts, each resting on the one before it.''
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:376:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:377:# ''The subjects.'' Specified in code.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:378:# ''Private authority.'' Specified in code, with the two custody rows owed.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:379:# ''Local sessions.'' The signer and the face supplier stand specified in code. The debt closes when the node's session open and the browser holder call them.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:380:# ''The gate, behind interfaces.'' Specified in code, with the bundle's root, the held Nexus root, the rings by face key and the sorter over proven facts owed.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:381:# ''One wire cutover.'' Node and browser dialers, gate, sorter and ring lookup move together, and the vessel-key proof paths retire in the same step.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:382:# ''Sibling carriage.'' The herm dial, the inner proof and the sibling peer id move to face scope.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:383:# ''The road's re-cut.'' The founding road's charter, wire and face slices state this shape.
