packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:1:/**
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:2: * floor-porch — the Nexus's floor at the porch: the release chain it answers a stranger with, and the floor blobs it
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:3: * names, each by a name the stranger brings.
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:4: *
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:5: *   GET /floor/<Nexus AID>   → the porch answer (`floor-answer`): the release rows this vessel's crossroads board carries,
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:6: *                              each with the charter's epoch lineage riding its record. Public by construction: the
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:7: *                              answer holds signatures and public keys, and a reader verifies every step itself.
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:8: *   GET /cas/<cid>           → a floor blob the chain's HEAD release names (its manifest and the two snapshots) and
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:9: *                              nothing else, re-hashed on the way out (a hearth mounts this route; a herm already
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:10: *                              carries `/cas` in its bulb face and lends it the same lane through `publicCasShore`).
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:11: *
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:12: * THE SILENT RUNG (pronaos#/the-rung-ladder). Every other path, an AID this vessel does not answer for, a wrong method and a
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:13: * cid the head release does not name draw the one CLOSED DOOR, byte-identical to the dispatcher's terminal refusal. A herm
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:14: * carries and presents the answer and signs nothing: the porch holds no key.
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:15: *
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:16: * A BOARD ROW NAMES NO BLOB UNTIL IT VERIFIES. The set of servable cids derives at each ask from the verified chain (lineage,
packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts:17: * seal, approval), never from a bare row, so a row any peer wrote onto the board cannot make the porch serve a private blob.
