packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:1:/**
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:2: * runNexusContract / runNexusAcceptCarriage / runNexusMembersList — the RAISE side of the operator MEMBERS-registry
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:3: * (the Kapae-antigen's ALLOW-twin). The founding kahu WRITE a quorum-signed `admit` / `revoke` onto the
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:4: * always-carried members BOARD; the READER (`members-board`) + the consult (`nexus-membership`,
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:5: * `carrierShareDecision`) fold it. This is the writer they were missing — the mirror of `runNexusKapae`.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:6: *
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:7: * TWO WAX-SEALS ride an ADMIT (membership-doctrine):
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:8: *   · the OPERATOR's own "accepts carriage" contract-sig (the contract-in). Either the joining operator produced
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:9: *     it out-of-band (`lares nexus accept-carriage` → a token supplied via `contractSig`), OR — the a-multitude-
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:10: *     of-one ceremony — the vessel HOLDS a persona whose per-Nexus leaf IS the admitted nym and self-signs with
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:11: *     that leaf. FAIL CLOSED: no valid contract-in → REFUSE. A Nexus cannot conscript an operator into
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:12: *     carriage; the operator consents first.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:13: *
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:14: * THE SUBJECT IS A PER-NEXUS LEAF, never a PersonaGroup root (`nexus-leaf`). The members board travels, so
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:15: * the nym it carries is published; a leaf presents a different key to each Nexus and the same key to one
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:16: * Nexus across a seal rotation, where a root would name the human's device-group on every island at once.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:17: *
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:18: * THE QUORUM SIGNS WITH THE SEATS' OWN KEYS (`held-quorum`, `seat-key-store`): a seat's key stands apart from
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:19: * every persona root and every leaf, so the charter publishes no root and no dialing key signs a quorum's act.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:20: *   · ≥ threshold founding-kahu quorum signatures (the steward act — identical to the antigen's).
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:21: * A REVOKE needs the kahu quorum ONLY (an uncooperative member cannot veto its own removal).
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:22: *
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:23: * TWO VAULTS, ONE ACT (kapae#/edge-hands). A Nexus whose seats rest in two vaults (a two-founder Nexus) signs no
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:24: * admit or revoke whole in either. `runNexusContractOpen` signs with every seat this vessel holds and hands back a
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:25: * PARTIAL (`nexus-partial`) that carries the whole act and writes no board; the other vault's
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:26: * `runNexusContractPartial` judges it against its own charter head and board, cosigns with the seats it holds
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:27: * only where the judge reads `ready`, and lands the act once it reads `complete`. The first vault lands the
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:28: * completed partial the same way. A stale head, a moved line, a replay or a foreign Nexus writes no signature and
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:29: * no board act. `aid` names a charter this vessel carries (a joint Nexus files under its own AID beside the seed).
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:30: *
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:31: * TRACK CONTRACTS, NEVER IDENTITIES: the writer takes an operator PUBKEY nym + (for admit) a carriage contract-sig.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:32: * No name / email / device / behavior is read, asked, or written — the FLOOR alone lands on the board.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:33: *
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:34: * FAIL CLOSED, at every shore (mirrors nexus-kapae):
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:35: *   · an unseated / quorum-short charter → REFUSE (nothing to root a quorum on); no board write.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:36: *   · fewer than `threshold` HELD seat keys that sit IN the seated roster → REFUSE; no sub-quorum entry.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:37: *   · an admit with no valid contract-in → REFUSE; never write a conscripted member.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:38: *   · an entry that does not COUNT against the seated roster → REFUSE; never write a dead admit.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:39: *   · a malformed nym → REFUSE.
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:40: *
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:41: * Meme: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-operator-contract
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:42: */
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:43:
packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts:44:import type { Repo } from "@automerge/automerge-repo";
